<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="sec-derivative-tables">
<title>Derivative Tables</title>

<introduction>
<remark>
<title>Prerequisites</title>
<p>Functions, limits, algebraic manipulation, trigonometric functions,
inverse trigonometric functions, exponential and logarithmic functions,
hyperbolic functions, implicit differentiation, and multivariable notation.</p>
</remark>

<remark>
<title>Learning Objectives</title>
<p>By the end of this reference section, the reader should be able to:</p>

<p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>recognize standard derivative notation;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>use constant, power, sum, difference, product, quotient,
          and chain rules;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>differentiate polynomial and rational functions;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>differentiate exponential and logarithmic functions;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>differentiate all six trigonometric functions;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>differentiate inverse trigonometric functions;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>differentiate hyperbolic and inverse hyperbolic functions;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>differentiate functions involving absolute value where appropriate;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>use logarithmic differentiation;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>perform implicit differentiation;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>compute higher derivatives;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>recognize derivatives of common composite functions;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>differentiate parametric equations;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>compute derivatives in polar form;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>recognize partial derivatives and gradients;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>compute Jacobians and Hessians;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>recognize directional derivatives;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>differentiate vector-valued functions;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>identify common derivative patterns used in differential equations,
          optimization, probability, and applied mathematics;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>avoid common sign, chain-rule, and domain errors.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</p>
</remark>
</introduction>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-derivative-notation-table-reference">
<title>Derivative Notation</title>
<p>For</p>

<p>
<md>y=f(x),</md>
</p>

<p>common derivative notation includes</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
f'(x),
}</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{dy}{dx},
}</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{df}{dx},
}</md>
</p>

<p>and</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
D_xf.
}</md>
</p>

<p>All represent the derivative with respect to <m>x</m>.</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-derivative-definition-reference">
<title>Derivative Definition</title>
<p>The derivative of <m>f</m> at <m>x</m> is</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
f'(x)
=
\lim_{h\to0}
\frac{
f(x+h)-f(x)
}{
h
}
}</md>
</p>

<p>whenever the limit exists.</p>

<p>An equivalent form at <m>x=a</m> is</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
f'(a)
=
\lim_{x\to a}
\frac{
f(x)-f(a)
}{
x-a
}.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-derivative-rate-change-reference">
<title>Derivative as Rate of Change</title>
<p>The derivative represents instantaneous rate of change.</p>

<p>If</p>

<p>
<md>y=f(x),</md>
</p>

<p>then</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
f'(a)
}</md>
</p>

<p>is the slope of the tangent line at</p>

<p>
<md>x=a.</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-constant-derivative-rule">
<title>Constant Rule</title>
<p>For constant <m>c</m>,</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}c
=
0.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-power-derivative-rule">
<title>Power Rule</title>
<p>For real exponent <m>n</m>, wherever the expression is differentiable,</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}x^n
=
nx^{n-1}.
}</md>
</p>

<p>For integer <m>n</m>, this is the familiar power rule.</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-constant-multiple-derivative-rule">
<title>Constant Multiple Rule</title>
<p>For constant <m>c</m>,</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}
[c f(x)]
=
c f'(x).
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-sum-derivative-rule">
<title>Sum Rule</title>
<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}
[f(x)+g(x)]
=
f'(x)+g'(x).
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-difference-derivative-rule">
<title>Difference Rule</title>
<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}
[f(x)-g(x)]
=
f'(x)-g'(x).
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-product-derivative-rule">
<title>Product Rule</title>
<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}
[f(x)g(x)]
=
f'(x)g(x)
+
f(x)g'(x).
}</md>
</p>

<p>A useful mnemonic is</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
(fg)'
=
f'g+fg'.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-quotient-derivative-rule">
<title>Quotient Rule</title>
<p>For</p>

<p>
<md>g(x)\neq0,</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}
\left(
\frac{f(x)}{g(x)}
\right)
=
\frac{
f'(x)g(x)-f(x)g'(x)
}{
[g(x)]^2
}.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-chain-derivative-rule">
<title>Chain Rule</title>
<p>For</p>

<p>
<md>y=f(g(x)),</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{dy}{dx}
=
f'(g(x))g'(x).
}</md>
</p>

<p>In Leibniz notation,</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{dy}{dx}
=
\frac{dy}{du}
\frac{du}{dx}.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-worked-chain-rule-reference">
<title>Worked Example: Chain Rule</title>
<example>
<title>Differentiate a Composite Power</title>
<p>Differentiate</p>

<p>
<md>y
=
\left(
(x+1)^2+3
\right)^4.</md>
</p>

<p>Let</p>

<p>
<md>u
=
(x+1)^2+3.</md>
</p>

<p>Then</p>

<p>
<md>y=u^4.</md>
</p>

<p>Differentiate:</p>

<p>
<md>\frac{dy}{du}
=
4u^3,</md>
</p>

<p>and</p>

<p>
<md>\frac{du}{dx}
=
2(x+1).</md>
</p>

<p>Therefore,</p>
<p><em>Solution.</em></p>
<p>
<md>\boxed{
y'
=
8(x+1)
\left(
(x+1)^2+3
\right)^3.
}</md>
</p>
</example>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-power-chain-rule">
<title>General Power-Chain Rule</title>
<p>For differentiable <m>u=u(x)</m>,</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}
[u(x)]^n
=
n[u(x)]^{n-1}u'(x).
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-polynomial-derivatives-reference">
<title>Polynomial Derivatives</title>
<p>For</p>

<p>
<md>p(x)
=
a_nx^n+\cdots+a_1x+a_0,</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
p'(x)
=
na_nx^{n-1}
+
\cdots
+
a_1.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-reciprocal-derivative-reference">
<title>Reciprocal Function</title>
<p>For</p>

<p>
<md>x\neq0,</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}
\left(
\frac1x
\right)
=
-\frac1{x^2}.
}</md>
</p>

<p>More generally,</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}
\left(
\frac1{u}
\right)
=
-\frac{u'}{u^2}.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-square-root-derivative-reference">
<title>Square Root</title>
<p>For</p>

<p>
<md>x&gt;0,</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}
\sqrt{x}
=
\frac{1}{2\sqrt{x}}.
}</md>
</p>

<p>For a differentiable inner function <m>u(x)&gt;0</m>,</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}
\sqrt{u}
=
\frac{u'}{2\sqrt{u}}.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-general-radical-derivative">
<title>General Radical</title>
<p>For suitable domains,</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}
u^{1/n}
=
\frac1n
u^{1/n-1}
u'.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-e-exponential-derivative">
<title>Natural Exponential</title>
<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}e^x
=
e^x.
}</md>
</p>

<p>For <m>u=u(x)</m>,</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}e^u
=
e^u u'.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-general-exponential-derivative">
<title>General Exponential</title>
<p>For constant</p>

<p>
<md>a&gt;0,
\qquad
a\neq1,</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}a^x
=
a^x\ln a.
}</md>
</p>

<p>For <m>u=u(x)</m>,</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}
a^{u}
=
a^u\ln(a)\,u'.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-natural-logarithm-derivative">
<title>Natural Logarithm</title>
<p>For</p>

<p>
<md>x&gt;0,</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}\ln x
=
\frac1x.
}</md>
</p>

<p>More generally, where <m>u(x)\neq0</m>,</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}
\ln|u|
=
\frac{u'}{u}.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-general-logarithm-derivative">
<title>General Logarithm</title>
<p>For</p>

<p>
<md>a&gt;0,
\qquad
a\neq1,
\qquad
x&gt;0,</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}
\log_a x
=
\frac{
1
}{
x\ln a
}.
}</md>
</p>

<p>For <m>u=u(x)&gt;0</m>,</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}
\log_a u
=
\frac{
u'
}{
u\ln a
}.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-sine-derivative-reference">
<title>Sine Derivative</title>
<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}\sin x
=
\cos x.
}</md>
</p>

<p>For <m>u=u(x)</m>,</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}\sin u
=
\cos u\,u'.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-cosine-derivative-reference">
<title>Cosine Derivative</title>
<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}\cos x
=
-\sin x.
}</md>
</p>

<p>For <m>u=u(x)</m>,</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}\cos u
=
-\sin u\,u'.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-tangent-derivative-reference">
<title>Tangent Derivative</title>
<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}\tan x
=
\sec^2x.
}</md>
</p>

<p>For <m>u=u(x)</m>,</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}\tan u
=
\sec^2u\,u'.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-cotangent-derivative-reference">
<title>Cotangent Derivative</title>
<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}\cot x
=
-\csc^2x.
}</md>
</p>

<p>For <m>u=u(x)</m>,</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}\cot u
=
-\csc^2u\,u'.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-secant-derivative-reference">
<title>Secant Derivative</title>
<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}\sec x
=
\sec x\tan x.
}</md>
</p>

<p>For <m>u=u(x)</m>,</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}\sec u
=
\sec u\tan u\,u'.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-cosecant-derivative-reference">
<title>Cosecant Derivative</title>
<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}\csc x
=
-\csc x\cot x.
}</md>
</p>

<p>For <m>u=u(x)</m>,</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}\csc u
=
-\csc u\cot u\,u'.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-quick-trig-derivative-table">
<title>Quick Trigonometric Derivative Table</title>
<p>
<md>\boxed{
(\sin x)'=\cos x
}</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
(\cos x)'=-\sin x
}</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
(\tan x)'=\sec^2x
}</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
(\cot x)'=-\csc^2x
}</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
(\sec x)'=\sec x\tan x
}</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
(\csc x)'=-\csc x\cot x
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-inverse-sine-derivative">
<title>Inverse Sine Derivative</title>
<p>For</p>

<p>
<md>|x|&lt;1,</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}\arcsin x
=
\frac{1}{\sqrt{1-x^2}}.
}</md>
</p>

<p>For <m>u=u(x)</m>,</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}\arcsin u
=
\frac{
u'
}{
\sqrt{1-u^2}
}.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-inverse-cosine-derivative">
<title>Inverse Cosine Derivative</title>
<p>For</p>

<p>
<md>|x|&lt;1,</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}\arccos x
=
-\frac{1}{\sqrt{1-x^2}}.
}</md>
</p>

<p>For <m>u=u(x)</m>,</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}\arccos u
=
-\frac{
u'
}{
\sqrt{1-u^2}
}.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-inverse-tangent-derivative">
<title>Inverse Tangent Derivative</title>
<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}\arctan x
=
\frac{1}{1+x^2}.
}</md>
</p>

<p>For <m>u=u(x)</m>,</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}\arctan u
=
\frac{
u'
}{
1+u^2
}.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-inverse-cotangent-derivative">
<title>Inverse Cotangent Derivative</title>
<p>Under the common principal-value convention,</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}\operatorname{arccot}x
=
-\frac{1}{1+x^2}.
}</md>
</p>

<p>For <m>u=u(x)</m>,</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}\operatorname{arccot}u
=
-\frac{
u'
}{
1+u^2
}.
}</md>
</p>

<p>Inverse-cotangent conventions vary between texts.</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-inverse-secant-derivative">
<title>Inverse Secant Derivative</title>
<p>For</p>

<p>
<md>|x|&gt;1,</md>
</p>

<p>a standard real derivative formula is</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}\operatorname{arcsec}x
=
\frac{
1
}{
|x|\sqrt{x^2-1}
}.
}</md>
</p>

<p>For <m>u=u(x)</m>,</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}\operatorname{arcsec}u
=
\frac{
u'
}{
|u|\sqrt{u^2-1}
}.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-inverse-cosecant-derivative">
<title>Inverse Cosecant Derivative</title>
<p>For</p>

<p>
<md>|x|&gt;1,</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}\operatorname{arccsc}x
=
-\frac{
1
}{
|x|\sqrt{x^2-1}
}.
}</md>
</p>

<p>For <m>u=u(x)</m>,</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}\operatorname{arccsc}u
=
-\frac{
u'
}{
|u|\sqrt{u^2-1}
}.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-quick-inverse-trig-derivative-table">
<title>Quick Inverse-Trigonometric Derivative Table</title>
<p>
<md>\boxed{
(\arcsin x)'
=
\frac{1}{\sqrt{1-x^2}}
}</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
(\arccos x)'
=
-\frac{1}{\sqrt{1-x^2}}
}</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
(\arctan x)'
=
\frac{1}{1+x^2}
}</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
(\operatorname{arccot}x)'
=
-\frac{1}{1+x^2}
}</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
(\operatorname{arcsec}x)'
=
\frac{
1
}{
|x|\sqrt{x^2-1}
}
}</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
(\operatorname{arccsc}x)'
=
-\frac{
1
}{
|x|\sqrt{x^2-1}
}
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-sinh-derivative-reference">
<title>Hyperbolic Sine</title>
<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}\sinh x
=
\cosh x.
}</md>
</p>

<p>For <m>u=u(x)</m>,</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}\sinh u
=
\cosh u\,u'.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-cosh-derivative-reference">
<title>Hyperbolic Cosine</title>
<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}\cosh x
=
\sinh x.
}</md>
</p>

<p>For <m>u=u(x)</m>,</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}\cosh u
=
\sinh u\,u'.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-tanh-derivative-reference">
<title>Hyperbolic Tangent</title>
<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}\tanh x
=
\operatorname{sech}^2x.
}</md>
</p>

<p>For <m>u=u(x)</m>,</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}\tanh u
=
\operatorname{sech}^2u\,u'.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-coth-derivative-reference">
<title>Hyperbolic Cotangent</title>
<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}\coth x
=
-\operatorname{csch}^2x.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-sech-derivative-reference">
<title>Hyperbolic Secant</title>
<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}\operatorname{sech}x
=
-\operatorname{sech}x\tanh x.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-csch-derivative-reference">
<title>Hyperbolic Cosecant</title>
<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}\operatorname{csch}x
=
-\operatorname{csch}x\coth x.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-quick-hyperbolic-derivative-table">
<title>Quick Hyperbolic Derivative Table</title>
<p>
<md>\boxed{
(\sinh x)'=\cosh x
}</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
(\cosh x)'=\sinh x
}</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
(\tanh x)'=\operatorname{sech}^2x
}</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
(\coth x)'=-\operatorname{csch}^2x
}</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
(\operatorname{sech}x)'
=
-\operatorname{sech}x\tanh x
}</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
(\operatorname{csch}x)'
=
-\operatorname{csch}x\coth x
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-inverse-sinh-derivative">
<title>Inverse Hyperbolic Sine</title>
<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}
\operatorname{arsinh}x
=
\frac{
1
}{
\sqrt{x^2+1}
}.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-inverse-cosh-derivative">
<title>Inverse Hyperbolic Cosine</title>
<p>For <m>x&gt;1</m>,</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}
\operatorname{arcosh}x
=
\frac{
1
}{
\sqrt{x^2-1}
}.
}</md>
</p>

<p>Equivalently, one often writes</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{1}{
\sqrt{x-1}\sqrt{x+1}
}.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-inverse-tanh-derivative">
<title>Inverse Hyperbolic Tangent</title>
<p>For</p>

<p>
<md>|x|&lt;1,</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}
\operatorname{artanh}x
=
\frac{1}{1-x^2}.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-inverse-coth-derivative">
<title>Inverse Hyperbolic Cotangent</title>
<p>On standard real domains,</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}
\operatorname{arcoth}x
=
\frac{1}{1-x^2}.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-inverse-sech-derivative">
<title>Inverse Hyperbolic Secant</title>
<p>For</p>

<p>
<md>0&lt;x&lt;1,</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}
\operatorname{arsech}x
=
-\frac{
1
}{
x\sqrt{1-x^2}
}.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-inverse-csch-derivative">
<title>Inverse Hyperbolic Cosecant</title>
<p>For <m>x\neq0</m>,</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}
\operatorname{arcsch}x
=
-\frac{
1
}{
|x|\sqrt{1+x^2}
}.
}</md>
</p>

<p>Notation and branch conventions can vary between texts.</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-absolute-value-derivative">
<title>Absolute Value Derivative</title>
<p>For</p>

<p>
<md>x\neq0,</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}|x|
=
\frac{x}{|x|}
=
\operatorname{sgn}(x).
}</md>
</p>

<p>At <m>x=0</m>,</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
|x|
}</md>
</p>

<p>is not differentiable.</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-sign-function-derivative-reference">
<title>Sign Function</title>
<p>For <m>x\neq0</m>,</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\operatorname{sgn}(x)
=
\begin{cases}
1, &amp; x&gt;0,\\
-1, &amp; x&lt;0.
\end{cases}
}</md>
</p>

<p>Thus</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}|x|
=
\operatorname{sgn}(x)
}</md>
</p>

<p>away from zero.</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-logarithmic-differentiation-reference">
<title>Logarithmic Differentiation</title>
<p>Logarithmic differentiation is useful when variables occur in both base and
exponent or when many products and powers are present.</p>

<p>If</p>

<p>
<md>y=f(x)&gt;0,</md>
</p>

<p>take logarithms:</p>

<p>
<md>\ln y
=
\ln f(x).</md>
</p>

<p>Differentiate implicitly:</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{y'}{y}
=
\frac{d}{dx}
\ln f(x).
}</md>
</p>

<p>Then solve for <m>y'</m>.</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-x-to-x-derivative">
<title>Derivative of <m>x^x</m></title>
<p>Let</p>

<p>
<md>y=x^x,
\qquad
x&gt;0.</md>
</p>

<p>Take logarithms:</p>

<p>
<md>\ln y
=
x\ln x.</md>
</p>

<p>Differentiate:</p>

<p>
<md>\frac{y'}{y}
=
\ln x+1.</md>
</p>

<p>Therefore,</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}x^x
=
x^x(\ln x+1).
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-general-variable-power-derivative">
<title>General Variable Power</title>
<p>For positive <m>f(x)</m>,</p>

<p>
<md>y
=
[f(x)]^{g(x)}.</md>
</p>

<p>Then</p>

<p>
<md>\ln y
=
g(x)\ln f(x).</md>
</p>

<p>Therefore,</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
y'
=
f(x)^{g(x)}
\left[
g'(x)\ln f(x)
+
g(x)\frac{f'(x)}{f(x)}
\right].
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-implicit-differentiation-reference">
<title>Implicit Differentiation</title>
<p>If <m>x</m> and <m>y</m> satisfy</p>

<p>
<md>F(x,y)=0,</md>
</p>

<p>differentiate both sides with respect to <m>x</m>.</p>

<p>Treat</p>

<p>
<md>y=y(x).</md>
</p>

<p>For example,</p>

<p>
<md>x^2+y^2=1</md>
</p>

<p>gives</p>

<p>
<md>2x
+
2y\frac{dy}{dx}
=
0.</md>
</p>

<p>Thus</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{dy}{dx}
=
-\frac{x}{y}.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-implicit-function-derivative-formula">
<title>Implicit Function Formula</title>
<p>If</p>

<p>
<md>F(x,y)=0</md>
</p>

<p>and</p>

<p>
<md>F_y\neq0,</md>
</p>

<p>then locally,</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{dy}{dx}
=
-\frac{
F_x
}{
F_y
}.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-higher-derivatives-reference">
<title>Higher Derivatives</title>
<p>The second derivative is</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
f''(x)
=
\frac{d^2f}{dx^2}.
}</md>
</p>

<p>The third derivative is</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
f'''(x).
}</md>
</p>

<p>The <m>n</m>-th derivative is</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
f^{(n)}(x).
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-worked-higher-derivatives">
<title>Worked Example: Higher Derivatives</title>
<example>
<title>Differentiate Repeatedly</title>
<p>Let</p>

<p>
<md>f(x)=x^4.</md>
</p>

<p>Then</p>

<p>
<md>f'(x)=4x^3,</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>f''(x)=12x^2,</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>f'''(x)=24x,</md>
</p>

<p>and</p>

<p>
<md>f^{(4)}(x)=24.</md>
</p>

<p>Thus</p>
<p><em>Solution.</em></p>
<p>
<md>\boxed{
f^{(5)}(x)=0.
}</md>
</p>
</example>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-inverse-function-derivative-general">
<title>Derivative of an Inverse Function</title>
<p>If <m>f</m> is differentiable and invertible and</p>

<p>
<md>f'(f^{-1}(y))\neq0,</md>
</p>

<p>then</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
(f^{-1})'(y)
=
\frac{
1
}{
f'(f^{-1}(y))
}.
}</md>
</p>

<p>Equivalently,</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
(f^{-1})'(x)
=
\frac{
1
}{
f'(f^{-1}(x))
}.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-parametric-first-derivative">
<title>Parametric First Derivative</title>
<p>If</p>

<p>
<md>x=x(t),
\qquad
y=y(t),</md>
</p>

<p>and</p>

<p>
<md>\frac{dx}{dt}\neq0,</md>
</p>

<p>then</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{dy}{dx}
=
\frac{
dy/dt
}{
dx/dt
}.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-parametric-second-derivative">
<title>Parametric Second Derivative</title>
<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}
=
\frac{
\dfrac{d}{dt}
\left(
\dfrac{dy}{dx}
\right)
}{
dx/dt
}.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-worked-parametric-derivative">
<title>Worked Example: Parametric Derivative</title>
<example>
<title>Differentiate Parametric Equations</title>
<p>Let</p>

<p>
<md>x=t^2,
\qquad
y=t^3.</md>
</p>

<p>Then</p>

<p>
<md>\frac{dx}{dt}=2t,</md>
</p>

<p>and</p>

<p>
<md>\frac{dy}{dt}=3t^2.</md>
</p>

<p>Therefore, for <m>t\neq0</m>,</p>
<p><em>Solution.</em></p>
<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{dy}{dx}
=
\frac{3t}{2}.
}</md>
</p>
</example>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-polar-first-derivative">
<title>Polar First Derivative</title>
<p>For</p>

<p>
<md>r=r(\theta),</md>
</p>

<p>with</p>

<p>
<md>x=r\cos\theta,
\qquad
y=r\sin\theta,</md>
</p>

<p>we have</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{dy}{dx}
=
\frac{
r'(\theta)\sin\theta
+
r(\theta)\cos\theta
}{
r'(\theta)\cos\theta
-
r(\theta)\sin\theta
}.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-vector-valued-derivative">
<title>Vector-Valued Derivatives</title>
<p>For</p>

<p>
<md>\mathbf{r}(t)
=
\langle
x(t),
y(t),
z(t)
\rangle,</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\mathbf{r}'(t)
=
\langle
x'(t),
y'(t),
z'(t)
\rangle.
}</md>
</p>

<p>The derivative is taken componentwise.</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-velocity-acceleration-derivative">
<title>Velocity and Acceleration</title>
<p>If</p>

<p>
<md>\mathbf{r}(t)</md>
</p>

<p>is position, then velocity is</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\mathbf{v}(t)
=
\mathbf{r}'(t).
}</md>
</p>

<p>Acceleration is</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\mathbf{a}(t)
=
\mathbf{r}''(t).
}</md>
</p>

<p>Speed is</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\|\mathbf{v}(t)\|.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-partial-derivative-table-reference">
<title>Partial Derivative</title>
<p>For</p>

<p>
<md>f=f(x_1,\ldots,x_n),</md>
</p>

<p>the partial derivative with respect to <m>x_i</m> is</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{\partial f}{\partial x_i}.
}</md>
</p>

<p>Other variables are held fixed.</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-gradient-derivative-table">
<title>Gradient</title>
<p>For scalar function</p>

<p>
<md>f:\mathbb{R}^n\to\mathbb{R},</md>
</p>

<p>the gradient is</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\nabla f
=
\begin{bmatrix}
\frac{\partial f}{\partial x_1}\\
\vdots\\
\frac{\partial f}{\partial x_n}
\end{bmatrix}.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-directional-derivative-reference">
<title>Directional Derivative</title>
<p>For unit vector <m>\mathbf{u}</m>,</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
D_{\mathbf{u}}f
=
\nabla f\cdot\mathbf{u}.
}</md>
</p>

<p>This gives the instantaneous rate of change of <m>f</m> in direction
<m>\mathbf{u}</m>.</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-jacobian-derivative-reference">
<title>Jacobian Matrix</title>
<p>For</p>

<p>
<md>F:\mathbb{R}^n\to\mathbb{R}^m,</md>
</p>

<p>with components</p>

<p>
<md>F_1,\ldots,F_m,</md>
</p>

<p>the Jacobian is</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
J_F
=
\begin{bmatrix}
\dfrac{\partial F_1}{\partial x_1}
&amp;
\cdots
&amp;
\dfrac{\partial F_1}{\partial x_n}
\\
\vdots
&amp;
\ddots
&amp;
\vdots
\\
\dfrac{\partial F_m}{\partial x_1}
&amp;
\cdots
&amp;
\dfrac{\partial F_m}{\partial x_n}
\end{bmatrix}.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-hessian-derivative-reference">
<title>Hessian Matrix</title>
<p>For twice differentiable scalar function</p>

<p>
<md>f:\mathbb{R}^n\to\mathbb{R},</md>
</p>

<p>the Hessian is</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
H_f
=
\nabla^2f
=
\left[
\frac{
\partial^2f
}{
\partial x_i\partial x_j
}
\right].
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-mixed-partial-reference">
<title>Mixed Partial Derivatives</title>
<p>Under appropriate regularity conditions,</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{
\partial^2f
}{
\partial x\partial y
}
=
\frac{
\partial^2f
}{
\partial y\partial x
}.
}</md>
</p>

<p>This is often called Clairaut's or Schwarz's theorem.</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-multivariable-chain-rule-reference">
<title>Multivariable Chain Rule</title>
<p>If</p>

<p>
<md>z=f(x,y),</md>
</p>

<p>where</p>

<p>
<md>x=x(t),
\qquad
y=y(t),</md>
</p>

<p>then</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{dz}{dt}
=
\frac{\partial f}{\partial x}
\frac{dx}{dt}
+
\frac{\partial f}{\partial y}
\frac{dy}{dt}.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-matrix-chain-rule-reference">
<title>Matrix Form of the Chain Rule</title>
<p>For differentiable maps</p>

<p>
<md>F:\mathbb{R}^n\to\mathbb{R}^m</md>
</p>

<p>and</p>

<p>
<md>G:\mathbb{R}^p\to\mathbb{R}^n,</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
J_{F\circ G}(x)
=
J_F(G(x))
J_G(x).
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-dot-product-derivative">
<title>Derivative of a Dot Product</title>
<p>For differentiable vector functions</p>

<p>
<md>\mathbf{u}(t),
\qquad
\mathbf{v}(t),</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dt}
(\mathbf{u}\cdot\mathbf{v})
=
\mathbf{u}'\cdot\mathbf{v}
+
\mathbf{u}\cdot\mathbf{v}'.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-cross-product-derivative">
<title>Derivative of a Cross Product</title>
<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dt}
(\mathbf{u}\times\mathbf{v})
=
\mathbf{u}'\times\mathbf{v}
+
\mathbf{u}\times\mathbf{v}'.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-norm-squared-derivative">
<title>Derivative of a Vector Norm Squared</title>
<p>Since</p>

<p>
<md>\|\mathbf{x}(t)\|^2
=
\mathbf{x}\cdot\mathbf{x},</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dt}
\|\mathbf{x}\|^2
=
2\mathbf{x}\cdot\mathbf{x}'.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-norm-derivative">
<title>Derivative of a Vector Norm</title>
<p>If</p>

<p>
<md>\mathbf{x}(t)\neq\mathbf{0},</md>
</p>

<p>then</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dt}
\|\mathbf{x}\|
=
\frac{
\mathbf{x}\cdot\mathbf{x}'
}{
\|\mathbf{x}\|
}.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-matrix-inverse-derivative">
<title>Derivative of Matrix Inverse</title>
<p>If <m>A(t)</m> is differentiable and invertible,</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dt}
A^{-1}
=
-A^{-1}A'A^{-1}.
}</md>
</p>

<p>This follows from differentiating</p>

<p>
<md>AA^{-1}=I.</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-determinant-derivative">
<title>Derivative of a Determinant</title>
<p>For differentiable invertible matrix <m>A(t)</m>,</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dt}
\det A
=
\det(A)
\operatorname{tr}
\left(
A^{-1}A'
\right).
}</md>
</p>

<p>This is Jacobi's formula.</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-logdet-derivative">
<title>Derivative of Log Determinant</title>
<p>For differentiable invertible <m>A(t)</m> with positive determinant,</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dt}
\ln\det A
=
\operatorname{tr}
\left(
A^{-1}A'
\right).
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-gradient-linear-form">
<title>Gradient of a Linear Form</title>
<p>For constant vector <m>\mathbf{a}</m>,</p>

<p>
<md>f(\mathbf{x})
=
\mathbf{a}^T\mathbf{x},</md>
</p>

<p>then</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\nabla f
=
\mathbf{a}.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-gradient-norm-squared">
<title>Gradient of a Quadratic Norm</title>
<p>For</p>

<p>
<md>f(\mathbf{x})
=
\mathbf{x}^T\mathbf{x},</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\nabla f
=
2\mathbf{x}.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-gradient-quadratic-form">
<title>Gradient of a Quadratic Form</title>
<p>For</p>

<p>
<md>f(\mathbf{x})
=
\mathbf{x}^TA\mathbf{x},</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\nabla f
=
(A+A^T)\mathbf{x}.
}</md>
</p>

<p>If <m>A</m> is symmetric,</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\nabla f
=
2A\mathbf{x}.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-hessian-quadratic-form">
<title>Hessian of a Quadratic Form</title>
<p>For</p>

<p>
<md>f(\mathbf{x})
=
\mathbf{x}^TA\mathbf{x},</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\nabla^2f
=
A+A^T.
}</md>
</p>

<p>If <m>A=A^T</m>,</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\nabla^2f
=
2A.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-gradient-least-squares">
<title>Gradient of Least Squares</title>
<p>Let</p>

<p>
<md>f(\mathbf{x})
=
\frac12
\|A\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{b}\|^2.</md>
</p>

<p>Then</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\nabla f
=
A^T
(A\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{b}).
}</md>
</p>

<p>The Hessian is</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\nabla^2f
=
A^TA.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-logistic-derivative-reference">
<title>Derivative of Logistic Function</title>
<p>For</p>

<p>
<md>\sigma(x)
=
\frac{1}{1+e^{-x}},</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\sigma'(x)
=
\sigma(x)
[1-\sigma(x)].
}</md>
</p>

<p>This derivative appears in statistics, dynamical systems, and machine
learning.</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-softplus-derivative">
<title>Derivative of Softplus</title>
<p>For</p>

<p>
<md>f(x)
=
\ln(1+e^x),</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
f'(x)
=
\frac{1}{1+e^{-x}}.
}</md>
</p>

<p>Thus the derivative of softplus is the logistic function.</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-gaussian-function-derivative">
<title>Derivative of Gaussian Function</title>
<p>For</p>

<p>
<md>f(x)
=
e^{-x^2},</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
f'(x)
=
-2xe^{-x^2}.
}</md>
</p>

<p>More generally,</p>

<p>
<md>f(x)
=
e^{-ax^2}</md>
</p>

<p>gives</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
f'(x)
=
-2ax e^{-ax^2}.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-normal-density-derivative">
<title>Derivative of General Gaussian Density</title>
<p>For</p>

<p>
<md>f(x)
=
\frac{
1
}{
\sigma\sqrt{2\pi}
}
\exp
\left(
-\frac{
(x-\mu)^2
}{
2\sigma^2
}
\right),</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
f'(x)
=
-\frac{
x-\mu
}{
\sigma^2
}
f(x).
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-power-exponential-product-derivative">
<title>Derivative of Power-Exponential Product</title>
<p>For</p>

<p>
<md>f(x)
=
x^ne^{ax},</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
f'(x)
=
nx^{n-1}e^{ax}
+
ax^ne^{ax}.
}</md>
</p>

<p>Factoring,</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
f'(x)
=
x^{n-1}e^{ax}
(n+ax).
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-exp-trig-product-derivative">
<title>Derivative of Exponential Trigonometric Product</title>
<p>For</p>

<p>
<md>f(x)
=
e^{ax}\sin bx,</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
f'(x)
=
e^{ax}
(a\sin bx+b\cos bx).
}</md>
</p>

<p>For</p>

<p>
<md>f(x)
=
e^{ax}\cos bx,</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
f'(x)
=
e^{ax}
(a\cos bx-b\sin bx).
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-x-log-x-derivative">
<title>Derivative of <m>x\ln x</m></title>
<p>For <m>x&gt;0</m>,</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}
(x\ln x)
=
\ln x+1.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-log-square-plus-constant-derivative">
<title>Derivative of <m>\ln(x^2+a^2)</m></title>
<p>For constant <m>a</m>,</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}
\ln(x^2+a^2)
=
\frac{
2x
}{
x^2+a^2
}.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-sqrt-a2-minus-x2-derivative">
<title>Derivative of <m>\sqrt{a^2-x^2}</m></title>
<p>Where defined,</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}
\sqrt{a^2-x^2}
=
-\frac{
x
}{
\sqrt{a^2-x^2}
}.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-sqrt-x2-plus-a2-derivative">
<title>Derivative of <m>\sqrt{x^2+a^2}</m></title>
<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}
\sqrt{x^2+a^2}
=
\frac{
x
}{
\sqrt{x^2+a^2}
}.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-log-sec-tan-derivative">
<title>Derivative of <m>\ln|\sec x+\tan x|</m></title>
<p>Where defined,</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}
\ln|\sec x+\tan x|
=
\sec x.
}</md>
</p>

<p>This identity is useful when deriving the antiderivative of secant.</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-log-csc-cot-derivative">
<title>Derivative of <m>\ln|\csc x-\cot x|</m></title>
<p>Where defined,</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}
\ln|\csc x-\cot x|
=
\csc x.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-general-composite-derivative">
<title>Derivative of a General Composite</title>
<p>For</p>

<p>
<md>y
=
F(G(H(x))),</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
y'
=
F'(G(H(x)))
G'(H(x))
H'(x).
}</md>
</p>

<p>Each nested layer contributes one chain-rule factor.</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-worked-nested-composition">
<title>Worked Example: Nested Composition</title>
<example>
<title>Differentiate Several Layers</title>
<p>Differentiate</p>

<p>
<md>y
=
e^{\sin(x^2)}.</md>
</p>

<p>Differentiate the outer exponential:</p>

<p>
<md>e^{\sin(x^2)}.</md>
</p>

<p>Differentiate the sine:</p>

<p>
<md>\cos(x^2).</md>
</p>

<p>Differentiate <m>x^2</m>:</p>

<p>
<md>2x.</md>
</p>

<p>Therefore,</p>
<p><em>Solution.</em></p>
<p>
<md>\boxed{
y'
=
2x
e^{\sin(x^2)}
\cos(x^2).
}</md>
</p>
</example>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-quick-core-derivative-table">
<title>Quick Core Derivative Table</title>
<p>
<md>\boxed{
(c)'=0
}</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
(x^n)'=nx^{n-1}
}</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
(e^x)'=e^x
}</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
(a^x)'=a^x\ln a
}</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
(\ln x)'=\frac1x
}</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
(\log_a x)'
=
\frac{1}{x\ln a}
}</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
(\sqrt{x})'
=
\frac{1}{2\sqrt{x}}
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-quick-derivative-rule-table">
<title>Quick Rule Table</title>
<p>
<md>\boxed{
(cf)'=cf'
}</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
(f+g)'=f'+g'
}</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
(f-g)'=f'-g'
}</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
(fg)'=f'g+fg'
}</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\left(
\frac fg
\right)'
=
\frac{
f'g-fg'
}{
g^2
}
}</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
(f\circ g)'
=
(f'\circ g)g'
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-derivative-tables-common-errors">
<title>Common Errors</title>
<subsubsection xml:id="subsubsec-forgetting-the-chain-rule">
<title>Forgetting the Chain Rule</title>
<p>In general,</p>

<p>
<md>\frac{d}{dx}
\sin(x^2)</md>
</p>

<p>is not simply</p>

<p>
<md>\cos(x^2).</md>
</p>

<p>The correct derivative is</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
2x\cos(x^2).
}</md>
</p>
</subsubsection>

<subsubsection xml:id="subsubsec-incorrect-product-rule">
<title>Incorrect Product Rule</title>
<p>In general,</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
(fg)'
\neq
f'g'.
}</md>
</p>

<p>The correct formula is</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
(fg)'
=
f'g+fg'.
}</md>
</p>
</subsubsection>

<subsubsection xml:id="subsubsec-incorrect-quotient-rule">
<title>Incorrect Quotient Rule</title>
<p>In general,</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\left(
\frac fg
\right)'
\neq
\frac{f'}{g'}.
}</md>
</p>

<p>Use</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{
f'g-fg'
}{
g^2
}.
}</md>
</p>
</subsubsection>

<subsubsection xml:id="subsubsec-forgetting-the-negative-sign-for-cosine">
<title>Forgetting the Negative Sign for Cosine</title>
<p>
<md>\boxed{
(\cos x)'
=
-\sin x.
}</md>
</p>
</subsubsection>

<subsubsection xml:id="subsubsec-forgetting-the-negative-sign-for-cotangent">
<title>Forgetting the Negative Sign for Cotangent</title>
<p>
<md>\boxed{
(\cot x)'
=
-\csc^2x.
}</md>
</p>
</subsubsection>

<subsubsection xml:id="subsubsec-forgetting-the-negative-sign-for-cosecant">
<title>Forgetting the Negative Sign for Cosecant</title>
<p>
<md>\boxed{
(\csc x)'
=
-\csc x\cot x.
}</md>
</p>
</subsubsection>

<subsubsection xml:id="subsubsec-confusing-inverse-trig-with-reciprocal">
<title>Confusing Inverse Trig With Reciprocal</title>
<p>
<md>\boxed{
\sin^{-1}x
=
\arcsin x
}</md>
</p>

<p>in inverse-function notation.</p>

<p>It is not</p>

<p>
<md>\frac1{\sin x}.</md>
</p>

<p>The reciprocal is</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\csc x.
}</md>
</p>
</subsubsection>

<subsubsection xml:id="subsubsec-missing-absolute-values-in-arcsec-and-arccsc-derivatives">
<title>Missing Absolute Values in Arcsec and Arccsc Derivatives</title>
<p>The standard real formulas contain</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
|x|.
}</md>
</p>

<p>Thus</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
(\operatorname{arcsec}x)'
=
\frac1{|x|\sqrt{x^2-1}}.
}</md>
</p>
</subsubsection>

<subsubsection xml:id="subsubsec-forgetting-absolute-value-in-u">
<title>Forgetting Absolute Value in <m>\ln|u|</m></title>
<p>The identity</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dx}
\ln|u|
=
\frac{u'}{u}
}</md>
</p>

<p>holds wherever <m>u\neq0</m>.</p>

<p>Using only <m>\ln u</m> restricts to <m>u&gt;0</m>.</p>
</subsubsection>

<subsubsection xml:id="subsubsec-differentiating-x-x-with-the-ordinary-power-rule">
<title>Differentiating <m>x^x</m> With the Ordinary Power Rule</title>
<p>The power rule alone does not apply because both base and exponent vary.</p>

<p>Use logarithmic differentiation:</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
(x^x)'
=
x^x(\ln x+1).
}</md>
</p>
</subsubsection>

<subsubsection xml:id="subsubsec-dropping-dy-dx-in-implicit-differentiation">
<title>Dropping <m>dy/dx</m> in Implicit Differentiation</title>
<p>If <m>y=y(x)</m>,</p>

<p>
<md>\frac{d}{dx}y^2</md>
</p>

<p>is</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
2y\frac{dy}{dx},
}</md>
</p>

<p>not simply <m>2y</m>.</p>
</subsubsection>

<subsubsection xml:id="subsubsec-assuming-differentiability-from-continuity">
<title>Assuming Differentiability From Continuity</title>
<p>Differentiability implies continuity, but continuity does not imply
differentiability.</p>

<p>For example,</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
|x|
}</md>
</p>

<p>is continuous at <m>0</m> but not differentiable there.</p>
</subsubsection>

<subsubsection xml:id="subsubsec-confusing-partial-and-total-derivatives">
<title>Confusing Partial and Total Derivatives</title>
<p>For <m>f(x,y)</m>,</p>

<p>
<md>\frac{\partial f}{\partial x}</md>
</p>

<p>holds <m>y</m> fixed.</p>

<p>If <m>y=y(x)</m>, then the total derivative involves chain-rule terms.</p>
</subsubsection>

<subsubsection xml:id="subsubsec-ignoring-matrix-multiplication-order">
<title>Ignoring Matrix Multiplication Order</title>
<p>For matrix-valued expressions, multiplication may be noncommutative.</p>

<p>For example,</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\frac{d}{dt}
A^{-1}
=
-A^{-1}A'A^{-1}
}</md>
</p>

<p>cannot generally be rearranged.</p>
</subsubsection>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-derivative-evaluation-workflow">
<title>Derivative Evaluation Workflow</title>
<p>A practical differentiation strategy is:</p>

<p>
<ol>
<li>
<p>identify the outermost operation;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>simplify algebra first when useful;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>classify the structure as sum, product, quotient, or composition;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>apply the appropriate rule;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>use the chain rule for every nontrivial inner function;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>preserve constants;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>simplify only after differentiating correctly;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>check signs in trigonometric derivatives;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>check domains for logarithms, radicals, and inverse functions;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>use logarithmic differentiation for variable exponents;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>use implicit differentiation when <m>y</m> is not isolated;</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>verify dimensions or units when differentiating physical quantities.</p>
</li>
</ol>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-09-derivative-tables-subsec-derivative-table-exercises">
<title>Exercises</title>
