</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Differentiate</p>

<p>
<md>f(x)=x\ln x.</md>
</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Differentiate</p>

<p>
<md>f(x)=x^x.</md>
</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Use logarithmic differentiation to differentiate</p>

<p>
<md>y
=
\frac{
(x^2+1)^3
\sqrt{x-1}
}{
(x+2)^5
}.</md>
</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Differentiate implicitly:</p>

<p>
<md>x^2+y^2=25.</md>
</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Differentiate implicitly:</p>

<p>
<md>x^3+y^3=6xy.</md>
</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Use</p>

<p>
<md>F_x/F_y</md>
</p>

<p>to find <m>dy/dx</m> from an implicitly defined curve.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Find the first four derivatives of</p>

<p>
<md>e^x.</md>
</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Find the first four derivatives of</p>

<p>
<md>\sin x.</md>
</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Find</p>

<p>
<md>\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}</md>
</p>

<p>for</p>

<p>
<md>y=x^4.</md>
</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>For</p>

<p>
<md>x=t^2+1,
\qquad
y=t^3-t,</md>
</p>

<p>find</p>

<p>
<md>\frac{dy}{dx}.</md>
</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>For the same parametric curve, find</p>

<p>
<md>\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}.</md>
</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>For</p>

<p>
<md>r=2\cos\theta,</md>
</p>

<p>compute</p>

<p>
<md>\frac{dy}{dx}</md>
</p>

<p>in polar form.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Find the gradient of</p>

<p>
<md>f(x,y)=x^2+3xy+y^2.</md>
</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Find the directional derivative of a given function in a specified unit
direction.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Find the Jacobian of</p>

<p>
<md>F(x,y)
=
(x^2y,e^{xy}).</md>
</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Find the Hessian of</p>

<p>
<md>f(x,y)
=
x^3+xy^2.</md>
</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Verify equality of mixed partials for a smooth polynomial.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Use the multivariable chain rule for</p>

<p>
<md>z=x^2+y^2,
\qquad
x=\cos t,
\qquad
y=\sin t.</md>
</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Differentiate</p>

<p>
<md>\mathbf{r}(t)
=
(t^2,e^t,\sin t).</md>
</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Given a position vector, compute velocity, speed, and acceleration.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Differentiate</p>

<p>
<md>\mathbf{u}(t)\cdot\mathbf{v}(t).</md>
</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Differentiate</p>

<p>
<md>\mathbf{u}(t)\times\mathbf{v}(t).</md>
</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Prove</p>

<p>
<md>\frac{d}{dt}
\|\mathbf{x}(t)\|^2
=
2\mathbf{x}\cdot\mathbf{x}'.</md>
</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Derive</p>

<p>
<md>\frac{d}{dt}
A^{-1}
=
-A^{-1}A'A^{-1}.</md>
</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Differentiate</p>

<p>
<md>f(\mathbf{x})
=
\mathbf{a}^T\mathbf{x}.</md>
</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Find the gradient and Hessian of</p>

<p>
<md>f(\mathbf{x})
=
\mathbf{x}^TA\mathbf{x}</md>
</p>

<p>when <m>A</m> is symmetric.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Find the gradient of</p>

<p>
<md>f(\mathbf{x})
=
\frac12
\|A\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{b}\|^2.</md>
</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Differentiate the logistic function</p>

<p>
<md>\sigma(x)
=
\frac1{1+e^{-x}}.</md>
</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Show that</p>

<p>
<md>\sigma'(x)
=
\sigma(x)(1-\sigma(x)).</md>
</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Differentiate</p>

<p>
<md>e^{-x^2}.</md>
</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Differentiate a normal probability density with respect to <m>x</m>.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Differentiate</p>

<p>
<md>e^{ax}\sin bx.</md>
</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Differentiate</p>

<p>
<md>e^{ax}\cos bx.</md>
</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Derive the product rule from the limit definition.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Derive the quotient rule from the product rule.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Prove the chain rule under suitable differentiability assumptions.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
